│ of supplemental vitamin E (400 IU daily) or placebo. Compliance was determined non-invasively from simultaneous      │
│ measurements of aortic flow and carotid pressure at baseline and after 4 and 8 weeks. RESULTS arterial compliance    │
│ increased by 37% at 4 weeks and by 44% at 8 weeks (P = 0.01) only in the vitamin E group and was independent of an   │
│ effect on arterial pressure. A rise was seen in 12/14 subjects. There was no significant change with placebo (+ 8%). │
│ CONCLUSIONS short-term vitamin E supplementation improves arterial compliance."}, {"study_index": 200, "title":      │
│ "Annus horribilis for vitamin E", "abstract": "In January 2005, we published a dose–response meta-analysis showing   │
