from 4 randomized, controlled trials and 3 case reports on adverse effects were identified. Study quality was rated fair
for the studies on cancer, cardiovascular disease, cataracts, or age-related macular degeneration and poor for the 
studies on hypertension. In a poorly nourished Chinese population, combined supplementation with beta-carotene, 
alpha-tocopherol, and selenium reduced the incidence of and mortality rate from gastric cancer and the overall mortality
